### Twemoji Country Flags (via country-flag-emoji-polyfill)

The desktop app may bundle `TwemojiCountryFlags.woff2` (a flag-only subset of
Twemoji) so Chromium-based engines that lack country-flag glyphs can still
render them. The font is loaded locally; it is not fetched from a CDN.

- Font artwork: [Twemoji](https://github.com/twitter/twemoji), licensed under
  [Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
- Loader package: [country-flag-emoji-polyfill](https://github.com/talkjs/country-flag-emoji-polyfill)
  (MIT), Copyright (c) 2022 TalkJS

Attribution required by CC BY 4.0: the flag artwork is from Twemoji; this
product uses a subset of that artwork in the bundled color font.

Other Rust and JavaScript dependencies retain their own licenses as declared
